SUMMARY:Chinedu Unaka LIVE at San Jose Improv
DTSTAMP:20260715T051906Z
DTSTART:20260715T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nChinedu U
	naka is a Los Angeles-based stand-up comedian\, actor\, and writer who has
	 quickly become one of the most exciting voices in comedy today. \nHe has 
	been featured on Don’t Tell Comedy\, Comedy Central Presents\, and the Ars
	enio Hall Show (Netflix is a Joke). His acting credits include guest roles
	 on hit TV shows like Abbott Elementary and Insecure\, as well as the feat
	ure film House Party. \nHis debut comedy album “Mostly Kidding” debuted at
	 #1 on iTunes\, and he co-hosts the award-winning podcast “Nosy Neighbors.
	” Timeout LA recognized him as “A Comic to Watch\,” and he has toured glob
	ally alongside comedy heavyweights including Damon Wayans\, Marlon Wayans\
	, Damon Wayans Jr.\, and Yvonne Orji. \nBorn and raised in Los Angeles\, C
	hinedu started doing stand-up while studying at UCSB. He later earned a Ma
	ster’s in Education from Loyola Marymount and worked as a public school sp
	ecial education teacher before pursuing comedy full-time. His smooth deliv
	ery and engaging style make him a crowd favorite wherever he performs. \nE
	vent Details\n\nDate: Wednesday\, July 15\, 2026\nShow Time: 8:00 PM PDT\n
	Doors Open: 6:30 PM PDT\nVenue: San Jose Improv\, 62 S Second St\, San Jos
	e\, CA 95113\nAge Restriction: 21+ Event — Valid ID required at entry\nTwo
	-Item Minimum: All guests must purchase a minimum of two food/beverage ite
	ms in the showroom\nNo Photography or Recording: Cell phone use\, photogra
	phy\, and video recording are not permitted during the performance\n\nAbou
	t the Venue\nThe San Jose Improv is one of the Bay Area’s most beloved com
	edy clubs\, nestled in the heart of downtown San Jose at 62 S Second St. \
	nAs part of the nationally recognized Improv Comedy Club chain\, the San J
	ose Improv delivers an intimate\, club-style experience where the stage fe
	els just steps away. The venue offers general admission seating on a first
